<title>USA: U.S. ethanol subsidy unchanged in tax deal.</title>
<headline>U.S. ethanol subsidy unchanged in tax deal.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The subsidy for ethanol was unchanged in the tax deal worked out Monday between Congress and the White House, congressional and industry sources said.</p>
<p>A Republican source said it would remain &quot;the current law.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;The status quo means we've lost nothing,&quot; an ethanol industry source said.</p>
<p>House Ways and Means Committee Chairman William Archer, a Texas Republican, had pushed to eliminate the subsidy.</p>
